=========================================================
11. BUILDER vs FACTORY METHOD
=========================================================

Factory Method

• Creates ONE object.
• Focus is object creation.
• Returns object immediately.

Example:

createVehicle()

----------------------------

Builder

• Builds complex object step-by-step.
• Focus is construction process.
• Multiple build steps.

Example:

setEngine()

setBody()

setSeats()

buildCar()


=========================================================
12. IMPORTANT INTERVIEW QUESTIONS
=========================================================

Q. Why Builder instead of constructor?

Answer:

Large constructors become difficult to read,
maintain, and extend.

Builder constructs objects step-by-step.


---------------------------------------------------------

Q. What is the Director?

Answer:

Director controls the construction sequence.
It knows HOW to build, but not the implementation.


---------------------------------------------------------

Q. Can Builder work without Director?

Answer:

Yes.

The client can directly call builder methods.

Director is optional but improves reuse.


---------------------------------------------------------

Q. Difference between Factory and Builder?

Answer:

Factory creates an object.

Builder constructs a complex object step-by-step.


